# Crux design

- Before building a screen, open its reference in `docs/design/screens/` (index in `docs/design/README.md`) and match layout, hierarchy, copy and colours. The references are plain HTML with inline styles: translate them to Tailwind and shadcn components; ignore the `<x-dc>`, `<helmet>` and `DCLogic` wrappers.
- Track 0 put the tokens in `src/app/globals.css`, but its `--crux-paper` is a cream #f7f4ef; the approved reference is #F3F4F6, so fix it. Tokens live in `src/app/globals.css` (keep in sync with `docs/design/tokens.css`). Use the CSS variables, never raw hex in components.
  - Cardinal `--crux-cardinal` #9D2235 (brand, active nav, primary emphasis)
  - Cruxy gold `--crux-gold` #F5B700 (anything Cruxy does or says)
  - Ink `--crux-ink` #111318 (text, dark panels, primary buttons)
  - Paper `--crux-paper` #F3F4F6, surface #FFFFFF, line #E3E5E9, muted text #5A606B
  - Team colours: Team 1 #0F7B6C, Team 2 #4F46E5, Team 3 #C2410C
- Fonts: Bricolage Grotesque (display, 600 and 800), Inter (body), IBM Plex Mono (numbers, citations, timers). Load with `next/font/google`.
- Layout: dark 248px sidebar with the lowercase "crux" wordmark on desktop; bottom tab bar (Today, Cases, Practice, Team, Cruxy) on phones. Every page works at 390px wide.
- Touch targets at least 44px. Text contrast at least 4.5:1. Real `<button>`, `<a>`, `<label>`.
- Cruxy's images are in `public/cruxy/` (transparent PNGs). The lamp (`cruxy-lamp.png`) is Cruxy's only small icon: Ask Cruxy button, drawer header, chat messages, phone tab. Never crop Cruxy to a face-only avatar.
- The floating Cruxy, the lamp and the moods are specified in the spec's Cruxy section and drawn in `docs/design/screens/Cruxy.html` and `CruxyMoods.html`.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.
